Return only: status, commit SHA, test summary, and confirmation the guard was seen to fail. Under 8 lines.

Task 5 fix round 1/5. Review came back Approved — your `bulk` force-null was explicitly endorsed as closing a real edge case (category switched away from Shoes with stale `bulk` state), not masking one. Two Minors to close.

FINDING 1 — the Fit chip row has no way back to `null`, and this one matters more than "Minor" suggests.

Every other new field in the sheet can return to unset: the Selects seed from `item.field ?? null` and map "Not set" back to `null`. Fit cannot — once a chip is tapped there is no deselect, so an accidental tap is permanent and a user can never say "I don't know how this fits".

⚠️ Why this is not cosmetic: a later plan gates its proportion rules on **what fraction of items have a non-null `fit`**, and treats `fit` as the user's answer rather than the model's. A chip row that can only ever add values inflates that measurement with taps nobody meant, and the gate then reads as coverage it does not have.

Make the Fit chips **toggle**: tapping the already-selected chip clears it back to `null`.

```tsx
onClick={() => setFit(fit === f ? null : f)}
```

