# Cutout Rotation Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** A garment photographed sideways or upside down ends up stored upright — Haiku drafts the rotation, the confirm screen shows it applied, and one button lets the user correct it before saving.

**Architecture:** Rotation is NOT a tag and NOT a DB column: it is baked into the stored cutout and thumbnail at confirm time, so every reader (closet grid, flat-lay, Haiku re-tagging, share cards) sees an upright item with no per-view work. The model returns `rotation` (degrees clockwise: 0/90/180/270) alongside the tags because "which way is up" is semantic (a belt lying flat IS upright; trousers lying flat are not) — a geometric rule cannot decide it. The client keeps the uploaded cutout as the base, previews `rotate(base, rotation)`, and on save re-encodes and upserts the rotated cutout + thumb over the same storage paths. The original photo is never rotated (it is the photo).

**Tech Stack:** Zod 4 + Anthropic structured outputs (`lib/ai/tagging-schema.ts`), canvas rotation on the client (`lib/images/`), Supabase Storage upsert in the existing Server Actions, Playwright WebKit e2e.

**Spec:** This document (decided in conversation 2026-09-16; EXIF orientation was verified to already work end-to-end — `e2e/capture-exif.spec.ts`).

## Global Constraints

- Branch `feat/cutout-rotation` from `develop`; PR into `develop`. Never merge without an explicit go.
- Full branch mutation review before push (memory: full-branch-review-before-pr).
- Few code comments: one note per surprising decision.
- `Test assets/` is never committed; e2e fixtures are the drawn `e2e/fixtures/garment*.jpg`.
- `npm run test:run`, `npm run lint`, `npm run build` green; e2e for capture specs green (`set -a; source .env.local; set +a; npx playwright test e2e/capture*.spec.ts`).
- Structured-output schemas go through `forStructuredOutput()`; no validation keywords.

